      "body": "## purpose\n\nfixes #56770\n\ncompressed-tensors mxfp4 checkpoints with `input_activations: null` (llm-compressor `MXFP4A16`) were always built as `CompressedTensorsW4A4Mxfp4()`. on sm100+ that picks `FlashInferMxFp4LinearKernel` and quantizes activations the checkpoint never declared.\n\n`_get_scheme_from_parts` now reads `input_quant` on the mxfp4 branch the same way the nvfp4 branch already does:\n\n- `input_quant is None` builds `CompressedTensorsW4A4Mxfp4(use_a16=True)`, which passes `activation_quant_key=None` to `init_mxfp4_linear_kernel`, so it stays on the w4a16 marlin path\n- mxfp4 activations keep the current w4a4 behavior\n- any other activation format raises, same as nvfp4\n\nthis only covers the dense linear path. the fused moe side is #55232.\n\n## why this is not a duplicate\n\n- #55675 reads the same activation declaration but only logs a warning. it doesn't change which kernel runs.\n- #55232 fixes the moe backend selection, not the dense scheme. both are needed, as @jlqibm noted on #56770.\n\n## test plan\n\n```\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/quantization/test_compressed_tensors.py -k mxfp4_scheme_selection_respects_input_quant -v\nruff check / ruff format --check (v0.14.0) on the three changed files\n```\n\nthe test also runs with this branch merged with current main (no conflicts).\n\n## test result\n\n```\ntest_mxfp4_scheme_selection_respects_input_quant[weight_only_w4a16] PASSED\ntest_mxfp4_scheme_selection_respects_input_quant[w4a4] PASSED\n2 passed, 55 deselected\n```\n\nwith the two source files reverted to main, both cases fail (`'CompressedTensorsW4A4Mxfp4' object has no attribute 'use_a16'`), so the test catches the bug.\n\nruff: all checks passed, 3 files already formatted.\n\nno gpu run. i don't have sm100 hardware, so there's no end to end eval on an mxfp4a16 checkpoint. the unit test checks which activation key reaches the kernel selector.\n\nai assistance was used for this change. i reviewed every changed line and ran the tests above.\n",
